mental to them this is  attacking so many different things out  there if they want to come back Knight  to c3  that's fine Knight to f6 you can  continue your development as normal now  the better move for them after you take  this pawn is to play Knight to e2 but  that's a really tough move for them to  find after that move then Knight to f6  another piece attacking or defending the  square here on e4 maybe now they attack  you exchange a material right here and  then knight c6 this is you have much  better active pieces in the game all in  all I would definitely be taking black  in this position so this is the winner  where variation one of the more common  variations you'll run up against in the  French defense because you're just going  against the main lines that white is  playing so if you're new to the French  defense or you're curious from White's  perspective what are some of the lines  that you could see hopefully this was a  good introduction to the winnower and  you have much more confidence going into  the French defense because it is a very  very sound defense it gives you a very  good  tacking options if you are black thanks  again for watching the video I'll see  you guys in the next one I'm gonna have  a lot more variations of the French  defense coming out so make sure you  check out the chess website comm for  more updates of the French defense
 

